      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222212",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following statement:\n\n> Given that $A$ and $B$ are sets, $A\u2229B^(\u2015) = A^(\u2015)\u222aB^(\u2015)$.\n\nA part of the proof showing that $A^(\u2015)\u222aB^(\u2015)\u2286A\u2229B^(\u2015)$ is given below.\n\n> $L1$: Suppose $x \u2208 A^(\u2015)\u222aB^(\u2015)$.\n> $L2$: Then, $x \u2208 A^(\u2015)$ or $x \u2208 B^(\u2015)$.\n> $L3$: As a result, $x \u2209 A\u2228x \u2209 B$.\n> $L4$: Thus, $\u00ac(x \u2208 A\u2227x \u2208 B)$.\n> $L5$: And so $\u00ac(x \u2208 A\u2229B)$.\n> $L6$: This is equivalent to $x \u2209 A\u2229B$.\n> $L7$: Hence, $x \u2208 A\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n> $L8$: Therefore, $A^(\u2015)\u222aB^(\u2015)\u2286A\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from line $L1$ by the definition of {{field-1}}\n\nLine $L6$ follows from line $L5$ by {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\n\nTo complete the given proof, we must additionally show that if $x \u2208$ {{field-4}} then $x \u2208$ {{field-5}}"
